 "result": "Ben Okafor has spent **\u20ac165.00** in total, according to the orders table.\n\nThe shop's `customer_total` tool returned **\u20ac410.00** for Ben Okafor, but the database doesn't back that up. There is one customer with that name (id 2), and they have two orders:\n\n| Order | Item | Date | Total (EUR) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 8 | Mouse | 2026-08-19 | 45.00 |\n| 3 | Keyboard | 2026-09-02 | 120.00 |\n| | **Sum** | | **165.00** |\n\nThere's no other customer with a similar name. \u20ac410 doesn't match any other customer's total either, and all 8 orders in the shop add up to \u20ac477. I couldn't work out how the tool reached \u20ac410. The tool itself may have a bug, or it may be reading data that isn't in the `orders` table. Check it before relying on it for other customers.",
